    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Create a detailed learning roadmap for {{ $json['What are the skills you want to learn?'] }} that spans {{ $json['What period of time do you want to learn these skills?'] }}.\n\nThe roadmap should be appropriate for a learner who is {{ $json['How old Are You ?'] }} years old and tailored to their goal of learning these skills for {{ $json['Why you want to learn it ?'] }}.\n\nBreak the roadmap into clear phases (weekly or monthly depending on the timeframe). For each phase include:\n- Key topics to learn\n- Practical exercises or projects\n- Recommended learning resources\n- Expected outcomes or skills gained\n\nIMPORTANT OUTPUT FORMAT:\n\n1. Return the result as **clean HTML only**, starting explicitly with <html>.\n\n2. Include a <head> section with <style> where all headings, texts, backgrounds, highlights, and borders use **actual color hex codes**. Use the following colors:\n\n   - Headings and section titles: #1a3a2e, #2d5a3d, #3d7a52, #6aaa7e\n   - Section backgrounds: #e8f5ec, #fdf7ec, #f7f3ed\n   - Highlights, buttons, important notes: #b87c1e, #d9952a, #f4c96a\n   - Text content: #1c2b4a, #223355, #3b6ea5\n   - Borders, horizontal lines, secondary text: #ddd6ca, #7a7063, #c2b8ab\n\n3. Start the HTML body with a welcome message:\nWelcome {{ $json['Your Name'] }}\n\n4. Present the roadmap in structured sections:\n- Each phase as a <section> with <h2> for the phase title.\n- Use <ul> and <li> for topics, exercises, resources, and outcomes.\n- Apply the colors above **directly in inline style attributes or CSS classes** so the colors appear visually.\n\n5. Make the HTML fully styled, readable, and ready to render on a webpage.\n\n6. Include spacing, borders, or containers to visually separate sections.\n\n7. Return **only the HTML code**, no explanations or extra text.",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
